Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Storage Domain Creation Fails
Symptoms: Domain creation fails with permission errors

Solution:

# On NFS server, check and fix permissions
chown -R 36:36 /exports/data
chmod -R 755 /exports/data

# Restart NFS services
systemctl restart nfs-server
exportfs -ra
Issue 2: NFS Mount Fails
Symptoms: Cannot mount NFS shares from RHVH hosts

Solution:

# Check NFS server firewall
firewall-cmd --list-services | grep nfs

# Test manual mount from RHVH host
mount -t nfs4 nfs-server-ip:/exports/data /mnt/test
Issue 3: Storage Domain Shows as Inactive
Symptoms: Storage domain appears but shows inactive status

Solution:

Check network connectivity between RHVM and NFS server
Verify NFS exports are accessible
Check RHVM engine logs: /var/log/ovirt-engine/engine.log
Issue 4: Performance Issues
Symptoms: Slow storage operations

Solution:

# Optimize NFS mount options in RHVM
# Use: vers=4,minorversion=1,proto=tcp,fsc

# On NFS server, tune NFS daemon
echo 'RPCNFSDCOUNT=16' >> /etc/sysconfig/nfs
systemctl restart nfs-server
Best Practices
Storage Domain Management
Separate Storage Types: Use different storage domains for data, ISO, and export functions
Monitor Space: Regularly check storage domain capacity and plan for growth
Backup Strategy: Implement regular backups of critical storage domains
Performance Tuning: Optimize NFS settings for your workload requirements
Security Considerations
Network Security: Use dedicated storage networks when possible
Access Control: Implement proper NFS export restrictions
Encryption: Consider NFS over TLS for sensitive environments
Maintenance Tasks
# Regular maintenance script for NFS server
#!/bin/bash
# Check NFS service status
systemctl status nfs-server

# Monitor disk usage
df -h /exports/*

# Check NFS statistics
nfsstat -s

# Verify exports
exportfs -v
